==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɒt|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{term|grotto||lang=en}}, by shortening, or {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|grotte|lang=fr}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|poetic|lang=en}} A [[grotto]].
#* '''1819''', {{w|John Keats}}, ''[[s:La Belle Dame sans Merci|La Belle Dame sans Merci]]'':
#*: She took me to her elfin '''grot''', / And there she wept, and sigh'd full sore, / And there I shut her wild wild eyes / With kisses four.

===Etymology 2===
{{back-form|grotty|lang=en}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~|grots}} {{context|British|lang=en}}

# {{context|slang|uncountable|lang=en}} Any [[unpleasant]] substance or material.
# {{context|slang|countable|lang=en}} A miserable person.

